Test rg47: a statement on an origin's line
// "NNN/ word" is the origin and then a statement, as DEC's macro writes it.
// A slash anywhere else in a statement divides, with or without blanks.
// Some lines separate the origin from its statement with a tab, as macro
// sources do.  cpp turns a tab into a blank, so run_regression.sh assembles
// this file a second time with -n, which keeps the tabs, and compares the two.
100/ cla                // 0100: a statement on the origin's line
    lac 30/ 2           // 0101: lac (030/2), not an origin
    (30/ 2)             // 0102: a parenthesized divide
    30 / 2              // 0103: blanks on both sides: divide
    30/2                // 0104: no blank after the slash: divide
110/	5               // 0110: an origin, then the word 5
.+7/	x,	hlt         // 0120: the origin is an expression, and a label follows
    lac x               // 0121: lac 0120
130 + 10/	cma         // 0140: blanks inside the origin's expression
150/ 160/ 5             // 0160: two origins, then a word
170/ // a comment after an origin
    hlt                 // 0170
stop
